{#- drift_check: a minion-side Salt schedule runs `state.apply test=True`
   every interval_minutes (+ up to splay_seconds, so the minions don't all
   hit the master at once) and writes the outcome as node-exporter textfile
   metrics (salt_drift_*). Prometheus alerts on them (pillar/prometheus.sls).

   textfile_dir: Debian's prometheus-node-exporter reads this directory by
   default (no --collector.textfile.directory flag needed) — verified on all
   minions 2026-10-18. It belongs to the node-exporter package, hence the
   require on that formula.

   timeout_seconds: while another state run holds the lock the script
   retries every 30 s; the timeout caps that wait plus the run itself
   (arrstack's dry run takes ~25 s). With enforce it caps each of the
   dry run, the repair apply and the second dry run.

   enforce: self-repair — on drift, run a real state.apply instead of only
   reporting. Off by default; turned on per minion in pillar where a
   re-apply is harmless (pillar/salt-minion-enforce.sls).

   enforce_window: limits enforce to a daily time window ("HH:MM" start/end
   in `timezone`, may wrap midnight). Outside it the check only reports.
   Empty start/end = always (homepage, monitoring, salt-master). Must be
   wider than interval_minutes + splay or a night can pass without a run.
   For hosts where a repair is disruptive but fine while nobody watches
   (arrstack, jellyfin: pillar/salt-minion-enforce-window.sls).

   beacons.service: Salt's service beacon, persisted to
   /etc/salt/minion.d/beacons.conf. Fires salt/beacon/<id>/service/<name>
   only on a status change (onchangeonly), not at minion start
   (emitatstartup off). The master's reactor (formulas/salt-master) starts
   a stopped service again if it is on its whitelist. delay_seconds must
   exceed the unit's StartLimitIntervalSec (default 10 s): systemd's own
   Restart= gets the first go, and once it gave up (start limit hit) the
   reactor's `systemctl start` would be refused until that interval passed.
   Off by default and currently on nowhere: it watched docker, and Podman
   has no daemon — each Quadlet unit restarts itself (Restart=always).

   version: the Salt version this host runs (version.sls: exact apt pin;
   upgrade.sls: the upgrade itself, only via orch.salt-upgrade). target
   empty = unmanaged (Tofu's "3008.*" pin stays). The pin goes into
   pin_file — the same file Tofu's cloud-init writes, taken over here.

   Master first: every host except master_id is capped at master_running,
   the version of the salt-master that renders the pillar (pillar sets it
   via test.version, which runs in the master). So until the master runs
   the target, the minions' pin and upgrade stay at the master's version —
   "master never older than its minions" holds in any apply order.
   effective: the result of that cap, computed below.

   packages: candidates; only those installed on the host are pinned and
   upgraded, all to the same version (they depend on salt-common =).

   upgrade: upgrade.sls hands the apt run to a transient systemd unit
   (outside the salt-minion cgroup — the package's postinst restarts
   salt-minion, and KillMode=mixed would kill an apt started by the minion
   itself mid-configure). It starts delay_seconds later, so the state's
   return reaches the master first, then waits up to idle_seconds until no
   job runs on the minion (proc_dir empty), else gives up. onedir_dir:
   salt-pip extras (pygit2, saltext.vault) live in <onedir_dir>/extras-<py>;
   if the upgrade changes the bundled Python, the script reinstalls them. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'drift_check': {
        'enabled': True,
        'enforce': False,
        'enforce_window': {'start': '', 'end': '', 'timezone': 'UTC'},
        'interval_minutes': 60,
        'splay_seconds': 300,
        'timeout_seconds': 900,
        'script': '/usr/local/sbin/salt-drift-check',
        'textfile_dir': '/var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter',
        'metrics_file': 'salt_drift.prom',
        'salt_call': '/usr/bin/salt-call',
        'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    },
    'beacons': {
        'service': {
            'enabled': False,
            'services': [],
            'interval_seconds': 10,
            'delay_seconds': 90,
        },
    },
    'version': {
        'target': '',
        'master_id': '',
        'master_running': '',
        'packages': ['salt-common', 'salt-minion', 'salt-master', 'salt-api',
                     'salt-syndic', 'salt-ssh', 'salt-cloud'],
        'pin_file': '/etc/apt/preferences.d/salt-pin-1001',
        'pin_package': 'salt-*',
        'pin_priority': 1001,
        'upgrade': {
            'unit': 'salt-upgrade',
            'script': '/usr/local/sbin/salt-upgrade',
            'delay_seconds': 15,
            'idle_seconds': 900,
            'proc_dir': '/var/cache/salt/minion/proc',
            'onedir_dir': '/opt/saltstack/salt',
            'apt_get': '/usr/bin/apt-get',
            'lock_timeout': 300,
        },
    },
} %}
{%- set salt_minion = salt['pillar.get']('salt-minion:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
{%- set v = salt_minion.version %}
{%- set effective = v.target %}
{%- if v.target and v.master_running and grains['id'] != v.master_id
      and salt['pkg.version_cmp'](v.target, v.master_running) > 0 %}
{%-   set effective = v.master_running %}
{%- endif %}
{%- do v.update({'effective': effective}) %}
